Modification. The generators add two glyphs to every face before deriving
anything from it: Catalan ŀ (U+0140) and Ŀ (U+013F), as composites of l and
L with the face's own middle dot (U+00B7). Upstream lacks the precomposed
letters, though it has the middle dot, so l·l already sets well; the
composites only make pasted text that uses U+0140 or U+013F render in this
face. Nothing else changes. The files above stay as published, and the
modification is applied by scripts/fonts.py (add_ldot). The OFL allows it,
and needs no renaming, since the face names no Reserved Font Name.
